# ---- Agent / tooling metadata ----
# The live WorkBuddy session logs are written under .workbuddy-ai/memory/. They
# are PUBLISHED, as the challenge's usage proof, at docs/session-logs/ (tracked).
# This directory stays ignored so agent tooling state, third-party skills with
# unknown licences, and any future token material do not ship. Refresh the
# published copy when a slice ships.
.workbuddy-ai/
.codebuddy/
.claude/
.cursor/

# ---- Git recovery debris (never commit git internals) ----
# A damaged or preserved .git tree must never be staged. Added 2026-09-30 after
# an object-store loss: see tasks/lessons.md and .workbuddy-ai/memory/2026-09-30.md.
.git.SURVIVING-RECORD*/
.git.broken*/
recovery-*/

# ---- Secrets & environment ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
secrets/
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# ---- Gate A spike output ----
# The probe records the endpoint, the response bodies it observed and the
# verdict. Bodies are redacted before they are written, but the file is still
# raw external response data and must not enter the repository. The harness
# itself (spike/gate_a/probe.py) is tracked; only its output is not.
gate_a_result.json

